# Morning AI Briefing — Implementation Spec

## Overview
Build a self-contained Python pipeline that generates a personalized daily AI/dev briefing as an HTML artifact (based on the v5 mockup design).

## Project Structure
```
morning-briefing/
├── briefing/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── gather.py       # Content gathering (web search + extract)
│   ├── rank.py         # Adaptive article scoring
│   ├── render.py       # Jinja2 HTML rendering from template + scored articles
│   ├── build.py        # CLI entrypoint: orchestrates gather → rank → render
│   └── config.py       # Loads config, exposes scoring weights, interests
├── templates/
│   └── daily-brief.html  # Jinja2 template (derived from v5 mockup)
├── config.yaml           # User interests, weights, decay params
├── pyproject.toml        # Python project metadata + deps
└── Morning AI Brief Mockup v5.html  # Design reference (read-only)
```

## Design Reference
The file `Morning AI Brief Mockup v5.html` is the visual baseline. Study it closely — the HTML template you produce should preserve its visual system exactly: dark theme, amber accents, monospace metadata rails, semantic color tags (green/blue/red/amber), compact panel layout, section structure, issue metadata footer, and the article-image mock slot.

Key design traits to preserve:
- Dark near-black background with subtle radial gradient and grid texture
- Amber (#f4a84d) primary accent, warm off-white (#f3eee5) text
- JetBrains Mono for rails/labels/eyebrows, Inter for body
- Top rail with issue path + status dot, bottom footrail
- Hero section: headline (mono, uppercase, amber), lede, 3 microcards
- Side stack with visual note, metadata idea, signal shape
- Signal band (theme line)
- Image treatment section + article image mock slot
- Two-column main: Top signals + For your build journey
- Interest strip: Rising topic + weighting/effect sidebar
- Second two-column: Agent/Hermes radar + One move today
- Triple bottom: Delivery path, Visual rules, Issue metadata
- Issue metadata: 4-column grid with Date, Published, Source window, Issue ID

## Template Variables (Jinja2)
The template `templates/daily-brief.html` should accept these variables:

```python
{
    "issue": {
        "number": 1,
        "date": "June 4, 2026",
        "day": "Wednesday",
        "time": "6:42 AM PT",
        "headline": "Headline text here",
        "lede": "Lede paragraph here",
        "theme_line": "Theme line copy here",
        "source_window": "Prior 18 hours",
    },
    "hero_cards": [
        {"eyebrow": "Top lane", "title": "...", "body": "..."},
        # exactly 3 cards
    ],
    "signals": [
        {"number": "01", "headline": "...", "tag": "Test|Track|Learn|Ignore", "why": "Why it matters text"},
        # 3-5 signals
    ],
    "build_journey": [
        "bullet point 1",
        "bullet point 2",
        # 3-5 bullets
    ],
    "rising_topic": {
        "name": "Topic name",
        "body": "Description paragraph",
    },
    "rising_details": [
        {"eyebrow": "Weighting", "title": "...", "body": "..."},
        {"eyebrow": "Effect", "title": "...", "body": "..."},
    ],
    "radar_items": [
        {"eyebrow": "Radar", "title": "...", "body": "..."},
        # 1-3 items
    ],
    "moves": [
        {"eyebrow": "Build path", "title": "...", "body": "..."},
        {"eyebrow": "Learn next", "title": "...", "body": "..."},
    ],
    "image_treatment": {
        "rule_title": "Rule text",
        "rule_body": "Rule body",
        "placement_title": "Placement text",
        "placement_body": "Placement body",
        "article_slot_eyebrow": "Article image mock slot",
        "article_slot_title": "Article slot title",
        "article_slot_body": "Article slot body",
    },
